# Where npm gets @testagentic/atf: a private package on GitHub Packages (npm.pkg.github.com), readable with a GitHub
# token of your own once the testagentic organization has given your GitHub account access to the package. This file
# is committed: never write the token itself here.
#
# The token: a GitHub personal access token (classic) with the read:packages scope. Set it as ATF_NPM_TOKEN in your
# environment, and as a secret in your CI (the Copilot cloud agent's setup steps read the repository's Agents secret
# ATF_NPM_TOKEN). npm reads it when it runs; nothing stores it.
#
# The scope line sends only @testagentic packages to GitHub Packages; everything else still comes from your usual
# registry. The token line is written ${ATF_NPM_TOKEN?}: with the variable unset, npm reads an empty token rather than
# the literal text, so every other npm command still works and only the framework's own install is refused
# (https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v11/configuring-npm/npmrc, "Environment variables can be replaced using ${VARIABLE_NAME}
# ... By adding ? after variable name they can be forced to evaluate to an empty string instead").
@testagentic:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${ATF_NPM_TOKEN?}
